## Assumption Challenge
Candidate vertices considered: owners, emitted digits, branch boundary events, hydrotope chambers, sliced-box thresholds, u-fibers, mirror pairs, route sidecars, and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices are proof emitters and quotient sidecars.  The quotient preserves the LRC random031 residual predicate only when emitted owner digits and the route sidecar can be reconstructed; scalar chamber volumes deliberately destroy that information and remain diagnostics.
